WEBVTT

00:05:57.961 --> 00:06:01.010
This was a lenticular photograph of Jerry Wiesner

00:06:01.010 --> 00:06:03.373
where the only thing that changed in the photograph

00:06:03.373 --> 00:06:04.716
were the lips.

00:06:04.716 --> 00:06:07.692
So when you oscillated that little piece

00:06:07.692 --> 00:06:10.922
of lenticular sheet with his photograph,

00:06:10.922 --> 00:06:12.935
it would be in lip sync

00:06:12.935 --> 00:06:15.174
with zero bandwidth.

00:06:15.174 --> 00:06:17.885
It was a zero-bandwidth teleconferencing system

00:06:17.885 --> 00:06:19.727
at the time.

00:06:19.727 --> 00:06:23.708
So this was the Media Lab's —

00:06:23.708 --> 00:06:25.401
this is what we said we'd do,

00:06:25.401 --> 00:06:27.976
that the world of computers, publishing,

00:06:27.976 --> 00:06:30.664
and so on would come together.